  "question": {
    "text": "Sun light falls normally on a surface of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and exerts an average force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>&nbsp;within a time period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> minutes. Considering a case of complete absorption, the energy flux of incident light is"
  },
